+  read_cache: |
+    `WatchableKV`'s `Read()` (unlike the plain `KV` returned by `NewStore`) serves current-
+    revision (`RangeOptions.Rev == 0`) `Range` reads from a bounded, per-store cache keyed by
+    the exact key/end/options, so bursts of identical reads (e.g. many replicas re-reading the
+    same small key set) skip the index/backend scan on repeat. Correctness depends on
+    invalidation running synchronously, inside the same critical section that already finalizes
+    a write's revision bump (see the write path in watchable_store_txn.go) and before a
+    snapshot-driven `Restore` releases its lock, rather than asynchronously (e.g. via the watch
+    channel) or on a timer: a write must be reflected before any reader — serializable or
+    linearizable — can possibly observe the revision it produced, or a stale value could be
+    served during a legitimate concurrent read. Any new mutation path added to this cell must
+    invalidate (or clear) the cache in that same synchronous fashion, not add a second way to
+    mutate the keyspace that bypasses it.
+
